From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:39:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally pay the compute bell group
 at pass end

With g16_compute_bell_group k, a compute record posted while at least
k compute commands are in flight skips its doorbell, and the k-th such
record rings for all of them, inside the publish pass. The default
g16_compute_onebell 2 already rings at most twice per pass: for the
first compute record and at the pass end. Once a pass publishes more
than 2k records, the group rings more often than onebell alone. On
1.1103 the group at 4 read 0.95 us per submission faster at 8 queued
and 4 to 8 % slower at 64 queued, where passes are long.

Add g16_compute_bell_late (runtime, default 0). At 1, with a group,
a compute record with at least k in flight is always posted without
a doorbell, and the end of the publish pass rings once if k or more
records are owed. The existing rule still rings owed records once
fewer than k compute commands are in flight, so none is left unrung
when the queues drain. A pass therefore rings at most once for its
deferred records. A pass that returns early at the publication
deadline rings every owed record first, as it already does for the
onebell records. The effect of the word has not been measured yet.

At 0, or with the group off, nothing changes. A new statistics line
reads "compute_bell_late: on W paid N exits N".

Assisted-by: LLM
